We can add progress callbacks to PackageManager and ResourceLoader.

Proposal
- PackageManager methods accept an optional progress callback:
  ```ts
  type PackageProgress = { source: string; phase: "resolve" | "install" | "update" | "done"; message?: string };
  ```
- DefaultResourceLoader accepts an optional onProgress callback. It passes that down to PackageManager and also emits its own phases for non package work.

Interactive mode can pass a handler that updates a loader or status line.

If you want, I can add a lightweight interface like:
```ts
interface ResourceLoaderProgress {
  phase: "extensions" | "skills" | "prompts" | "themes" | "context" | "system" | "package";
  message: string;
}
```

Confirm which shape you want.

